# Walk until a block is within mining reach. It is a skill of its own so that a
# failed search is ONE failure of the caller's rule: three failed explores
# inside this frame (the per-rule cap) fail it with not_found, and the caller
# then falls through to its next rule, see find_ore. It serves any block; only
# `explore(stone)` is given a short budget (300 ticks a call, so three failed
# calls end in 45 seconds): stone under flat ground is dug for (`find_stone`),
# and walking the surface for it is the last resort of `get_cobblestone`. Every
# other target keeps the full 1200-tick call.
skill search_surface(block: block)
  doc "Explore the surface until the given block is within mining reach; fails not_found when exploring runs out."
  rules:
    near($block, 5) -> done
    true -> explore($block)
